    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022-sch-1-sec-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 At the end of section 13G",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022#sch-1-sec-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(1A) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nSection 80U deals with civil penalty provisions in this Act.\n\n(2) The amount of the penalty for a contravention of subsection (1) by\na person other than a body corporate is an amount not more than\n$2,500,000.\n\n(3) The amount of the penalty for a contravention of subsection (1) by\na body corporate is an amount not more than the greater of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) $50,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any related body corporate, have\nobtained directly or indirectly and that is reasonably\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Legislation Amendment (Enforcement and Other Measures)\nAct 2022\nNo. 83, 2022\n\nattributable to the conduct constituting the contravention—3\ntimes the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—30%\nof the adjusted turnover of the body corporate during the\nbreach turnover period for the contravention.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) applies despite paragraph 82(5)(a) of the Regulatory\nPowers Act.\n\n(5) For the purposes of paragraph (3)(c), the adjusted turnover of a\nbody corporate during a period is the sum of the values of all the\nsupplies that the body corporate, and any related body corporate,\nhave made, or are likely to make, during the period, other than:\n\n(a) supplies made from any of those bodies corporate to any\nother of those bodies corporate; or\n\n(b) supplies that are input taxed; or\n\n(c) supplies that are not for consideration (and are not taxable\nsupplies under section 72-5 of the A New Tax System (Goods\nand Services Tax) Act 1999); or\n\n(d) supplies that are not made in connection with an enterprise\nthat the body corporate carries on; or\n\n(e) supplies that are not connected with the indirect tax zone.\n\n(6) Expressions used in subsection (5) that are also used in the A New\nTax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 have the same\nmeaning as in that Act.\n\n(7) For the purposes of paragraph (3)(c), the breach turnover period\nfor a contravention means the longer of the following periods:\n\n(a) the period of 12 months ending at the end of the month in\nwhich the contravention ceased, or proceedings in relation to\nthe contravention were instituted (whichever is earlier);\n\n(b) the period:\n\n(i) starting at the beginning of the month in which the\ncontravention occurred or began occurring; and\n\n(ii) ending at the same time as the period determined under\nparagraph (a).",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(1A) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nSection 80U deals with civil penalty provisions in this Act.\n\n(2) The amount of the penalty for a contravention of subsection (1) by\na person other than a body corporate is an amount not more than\n$2,500,000.\n\n(3) The amount of the penalty for a contravention of subsection (1) by\na body corporate is an amount not more than the greater of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) $50,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any related body corporate, have\nobtained directly or indirectly and that is reasonably\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Legislation Amendment (Enforcement and Other Measures)\nAct 2022\nNo. 83, 2022\n\nattributable to the conduct constituting the contravention—3\ntimes the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—30%\nof the adjusted turnover of the body corporate during the\nbreach turnover period for the contravention.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) applies despite paragraph 82(5)(a) of the Regulatory\nPowers Act.\n\n(5) For the purposes of paragraph (3)(c), the adjusted turnover of a\nbody corporate during a period is the sum of the values of all the\nsupplies that the body corporate, and any related body corporate,\nhave made, or are likely to make, during the period, other than:\n\n(a) supplies made from any of those bodies corporate to any\nother of those bodies corporate; or\n\n(b) supplies that are input taxed; or\n\n(c) supplies that are not for consideration (and are not taxable\nsupplies under section 72-5 of the A New Tax System (Goods\nand Services Tax) Act 1999); or\n\n(d) supplies that are not made in connection with an enterprise\nthat the body corporate carries on; or\n\n(e) supplies that are not connected with the indirect tax zone.\n\n(6) Expressions used in subsection (5) that are also used in the A New\nTax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 have the same\nmeaning as in that Act.\n\n(7) For the purposes of paragraph (3)(c), the ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022-sch-1-sec-14-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022-sch-1-sec-14-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022-sch-1-sec-14-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022-sch-1-sec-14-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022-sch-1-sec-14-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022-sch-1-sec-14-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022-sch-1-sec-14-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022#sch-1-sec-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 At the end of section 13G",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(1A) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nSection 80U deals with civil penalty provisions in this Act.\n\n(2) The amount of the penalty for a contravention of subsection (1) by\na person other than a body corporate is an amount not more than\n$2,500,000.\n\n(3) The amount of the penalty for a contravention of subsection (1) by\na body corporate is an amount not more than the greater of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) $50,000,000;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any related body corporate, have\nobtained directly or indirectly and that is reasonably\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nPrivacy Legislation Amendment (Enforcement and Other Measures)\nAct 2022\nNo. 83, 2022\n\nattributable to the conduct constituting the contravention—3\ntimes the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—30%\nof the adjusted turnover of the body corporate during the\nbreach turnover period for the contravention.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) applies despite paragraph 82(5)(a) of the Regulatory\nPowers Act.\n\n(5) For the purposes of paragraph (3)(c), the adjusted turnover of a\nbody corporate during a period is the sum of the values of all the\nsupplies that the body corporate, and any related body corporate,\nhave made, or are likely to make, during the period, other than:\n\n(a) supplies made from any of those bodies corporate to any\nother of those bodies corporate; or\n\n(b) supplies that are input taxed; or\n\n(c) supplies that are not for consideration (and are not taxable\nsupplies under section 72-5 of the A New Tax System (Goods\nand Services Tax) Act 1999); or\n\n(d) supplies that are not made in connection with an enterprise\nthat the body corporate carries on; or\n\n(e) supplies that are not connected with the indirect tax zone.\n\n(6) Expressions used in subsection (5) that are also used in the A New\nTax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 have the same\nmeaning as in that Act.\n\n(7) For the purposes of paragraph (3)(c), the breach turnover period\nfor a contravention means the longer of the following periods:\n\n(a) the period of 12 months ending at the end of the month in\nwhich the contravention ceased, or proceedings in relation to\nthe contravention were instituted (whichever is earlier);\n\n(b) the period:\n\n(i) starting at the beginning of the month in which the\ncontravention occurred or began occurring; and\n\n(ii) ending at the same time as the period determined under\nparagraph (a)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-enforcement-and-other-measures-act-2022-sch-1-sec-14-ss-1a",
